items.summary:
❗️Ukraine plans to deploy its own missile defense system FREYJA as early as December, Zelenskyy said.
▪️Russia currently produces about 140 ballistic missiles per month. To guarantee the destruction of that number, NATO rules require twice as many interceptors — 280 missiles;
▪️At the same time, even obtaining 100 missiles per month remains an extremely difficult task;
▪️Ukraine aims to receive 100–120 Patriot missiles per month during the coldest months from U.S. stocks and production, from European countries, and from partners in the Middle East;
▪️In parallel, Ukraine, together with companies from ten countries, is developing its own missile defense system FREYJA;
▪️The main parts of this system are the launcher and the missile. We have them. This is Ukrainian production.
